econd identity over an existing one. An app that minted under its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"own key and later switches to the helper silently gives every existing user"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a new identity, because the two keys never collide."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"Accessibility","anchor":"Accessibility","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeychainKeyValueStore\/Accessibility\/afterFirstUnlockThisDeviceOnly","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is tuned for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"device-bound identifiers: items stay accessible in the background after"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"first unlock but are excluded from iCloud Keychain sync and device-to-device"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"migration. Choose a stricter level ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeychainKeyValueStore\/Accessibility\/whenUnlockedThisDeviceOnly","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeychainKeyValueStore\/Accessibility\/whenPasscodeSetThisDeviceOnly","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") for sensitive material;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the protocol’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" surface is fine for short opaque tokens but not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"designed for secrets that require Face ID \/ Touch ID gating."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"Sandboxing & entitlements (macOS)","anchor":"Sandboxing--entitlements-macOS","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This store uses the data-protection keychain"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"kSecUseDataProtectionKeychain"},{"type":"text","text":"), so it "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"never"}]},{"type":"text","text":" triggers a user-facing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"prompt: no legacy “Always Allow \/ Deny” dialog, no prompt on a locked"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keychain, and — because no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"kSecAttrAccessControl"},{"type":"text","text":" is requested — no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Touch ID \/ Face ID \/ password challenge."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"sandboxed"}]},{"type":"text","text":" macOS app must still be entitled to use that keychain. It"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"needs either an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"application-identifier"},{"type":"text","text":" entitlement (Xcode adds this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"automatically for provisioning-profile–signed builds) or an explicit"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"keychain-access-groups"},{"type":"text","text":" entry. Without one, "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeychainKeyValueStore\/setValue(_:for:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" returns"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"type":"text","text":" and logs "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"errSecMissingEntitlement"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OSStatus"},{"type":"text","text":" −34018). This is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"build\/signing condition surfaced at runtime, "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}]},{"type":"text","text":" a user prompt:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["<key>keychain-access-groups<\/key>","<array>","    <string>$(AppIdentifierPrefix)com.example.myapp<\/string>","<\/array>"],"syntax":"xml"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"iOS \/ iPadOS \/ tvOS \/ watchOS only have the data-protection keychain and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"supply the access group implicitly — no extra entitlement is required."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"Which entitlement, for privacy","anchor":"Which-entitlement-for-privacy","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Encryption, this-device-only accessibility, iCloud-sync exclusion, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"backup exclusion are identical whichever path you take — the access group"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only governs "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"which of your own apps"}]},{"type":"text","text":" can read an item, never third"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"parties or the cloud. For app-private identifiers, in order of strictness:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Most private:","type":"text"}]},{"text":" a provisioning-profile–signed build with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"accessGroup: nil"},{"text":", relying on the implicit ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"application-identifier"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"group (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<TeamPrefix>.<bundle-id>"},{"text":"). No other app — even one you sign","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"under the same team — can ever be entitled to it. Mirrors the iOS","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"default exactly; zero sharing surface.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Practically equivalent:","type":"text"}]},{"text":" a ","type":"text"},{"type":"co